  "research_question": "Establish the theorem chain of 'Auditable Theory-to-Paper Pipelines for AI-Assisted Formal Mathematics'. Large formal-mathematics projects increasingly use AI agents for drafting, review, theorem search, and manuscript preparation. Ungated agent output, however, can create theorem-looking but content-poor edits, stale source references, duplicated submission routes, and premature paper promotion. We report an auditable theory-to-paper pipeline used around a Lean-backed BEDC source workspace and an automath publication workspace. The pipeline separates source development, intake packets, active paper directories, AI review loops, deterministic gates, and human promotion decisions. Its central rule is that AI output is advisory: load-bearing mathematical and submission claims must be tied to source paths, command logs, deterministic checks, and human-approved promotion. Four case studies illustrate the gates: intake isolation, overlap/submitted blocking, fake-extension rejection, and artifact",
  "target_journal_bar": "A submission to CICM presentation-only / mathematical software workshop route must have a coherent central scope, complete proofs for all in-scope claims, and notation compatible with the journal's standards.",
